clean all-three games: 5,333 across 386 dates (clusters)

=== cluster-robust (by date) pairwise DM + 90% CI of Brier difference ===
  Kalshi - Polymarket: ΔBrier=-0.226e-3  clustSE=0.170e-3  z=-1.33 p=0.184  90%CI=(-0.506,+0.054)e-3  |CI|max=0.506e-3 = 2.25pt
  Kalshi - Sportsbook: ΔBrier=-0.008e-3  clustSE=0.129e-3  z=-0.06 p=0.950  90%CI=(-0.221,+0.205)e-3  |CI|max=0.221e-3 = 1.49pt
  Polymarket - Sportsbook: ΔBrier=+0.218e-3  clustSE=0.182e-3  z=+1.20 p=0.231  90%CI=(-0.081,+0.517)e-3  |CI|max=0.517e-3 = 2.27pt

=== equivalence margins, translated to the probability scale ===
  ΔBrier = ε² for a systematic offset ε, so a margin δ admits √δ:
    δ=0.11e-3 -> 1.05pt   δ=0.44e-3 -> 2.10pt   δ=0.99e-3 -> 3.15pt   δ=1.00e-3 -> 3.16pt

  Economic anchor: an edge below (taker cost × price) cannot be monetised.
  All-in taker cost 4.2% of notional [immediacy.log].
    price 0.25 -> breakeven edge 1.05pt -> δ=0.110e-3
    price 0.50 -> breakeven edge 2.10pt -> δ=0.441e-3
    price 0.75 -> breakeven edge 3.15pt -> δ=0.992e-3
  The pre-stated δ=1.0e-3 coincides with the anchor at favourite prices (p≈0.75);
  it was fixed before these comparisons and is not re-chosen here.

=== TOST verdicts: equivalent at δ iff the 90% CI lies inside ±δ ===
  pair                          |CI|max         p=0.25      p=0.50      p=0.75  pre-stated
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Kalshi - Polymarket          0.506e-3             NO          NO         yes         yes
  Kalshi - Sportsbook          0.221e-3             NO         yes         yes         yes
  Polymarket - Sportsbook      0.517e-3             NO          NO         yes         yes

  A 'NO' at the tighter anchors reports the measurement's power, not a
  difference between venues: it means the comparison stops resolving below
  an edge only a zero-cost participant could ever act on.

=== the size of the difference, against the size of the skill ===
  source          Brier      UNC  DSC (skill)        MCB
  Kalshi         0.2196   0.2500        31.7e-3      1.31e-3
  Polymarket     0.2198   0.2500        31.5e-3      1.33e-3
  Sportsbook     0.2196   0.2500        31.9e-3      1.45e-3

  mean discrimination (the skill any venue has): 31.7e-3
  widest pairwise 90% bound:                     0.52e-3
  -> the venues' accuracy differs by at most 1.6% of the skill any of
     them has, and their miscalibration differs by less than that.
  This is the framing the result deserves: not '0.2196 vs 0.2198, a small
  number among small numbers', but 'indistinguishable to within 2% of
  everything they know'.

=== block bootstrap: 59 weekly blocks, 4,000 resamples ===
  distribution-free companion to the analytic TOST interval above
  pair                                 analytic 90% CI          bootstrap 90% CI   |CI|max   verdict at 1e-3
  Kals - Polymarket                   (-0.51,+0.05)e-3          (-0.52,+0.05)e-3     0.52   EQUIV
  Kals - Sportsbook                   (-0.22,+0.20)e-3          (-0.25,+0.25)e-3     0.25   EQUIV
  Poly - Sportsbook                   (-0.08,+0.52)e-3          (-0.03,+0.49)e-3     0.49   EQUIV
  The two intervals agree closely and give the same verdict, so the
  equivalence result is not an artifact of the normal approximation or
  of the cluster-SE formula.

