  SEs x1000, with the G/(G-1) correction; p from t(G-1)

  Kalshi - Polymarket: dBrier=-0.226e-3
    cluster level              G       SE       t       p   |CI90|max
    iid (no clustering)     5333    0.139   -1.63   0.103        0.45
    league x date            859    0.168   -1.35   0.179        0.50
    date (headline)          386    0.170   -1.33   0.185        0.51
    week                      59    0.173   -1.31   0.196        0.51
    month                     15    0.155   -1.46   0.167        0.48
    home team                271    0.144   -1.57   0.118        0.46

  Kalshi - Sportsbook: dBrier=-0.008e-3
    cluster level              G       SE       t       p   |CI90|max
    iid (no clustering)     5333    0.125   -0.06   0.948        0.21
    league x date            859    0.127   -0.06   0.949        0.22
    date (headline)          386    0.130   -0.06   0.950        0.22
    week                      59    0.156   -0.05   0.959        0.26
    month                     15    0.156   -0.05   0.959        0.26
    home team                271    0.121   -0.07   0.947        0.21

  Polymarket - Sportsbook: dBrier=+0.218e-3
    cluster level              G       SE       t       p   |CI90|max
    iid (no clustering)     5333    0.151   +1.44   0.150        0.47
    league x date            859    0.182   +1.20   0.230        0.52
    date (headline)          386    0.182   +1.20   0.232        0.52
    week                      59    0.160   +1.36   0.179        0.48
    month                     15    0.149   +1.47   0.165        0.46
    home team                271    0.147   +1.49   0.138        0.46

  Read: no level crosses alpha=.05 on any pair, and the WIDEST 90% bound at
  any level is roughly half the pre-stated delta=1.0e-3 — so the equivalence
  verdict is the same however the dependence is modelled. Clustering costs
  10-25% of SE against iid, and coarsening past date buys little: week and
  month are slightly wider on the two Kalshi pairs and slightly narrower on
  P-B, i.e. noise, not a missed dependence. Team clustering gives SMALLER SEs
  than date throughout, so no per-team shock is escaping the headline spec.
  D4's refusal of two-way date x league stands on its own grounds (G=7); this
  table shows the variance estimator is insensitive in any case.

